  "commentary": {
    "market_commentary": "The SSY Pacific Capesize Index edged higher 14 points from last week to 3,663 in its first weekly increase this year. SSY’s assessed W.Australia-China iron ore spot voyage rate has lowered $0.20/t to $6.20/t. The round-voyage is down $150/day on the week to $2,500/ day, still at the lowest level since the week to 10 February 2020.",
    "index_notes": "The Pacific Capesize Index started at 5,000 points on 27 December 1995 and has since been subject to periodic updating to reflect changing trade patterns. The latest update was on 17 July 2015.",
    "contact_info": "For more information contact Alastair Stevenson/David Beard"
  },
